Choose the deterministic tool for the requested operation. Return only {"tool_name":"registered_name"}.

Input data:
{
  "available_tools": {
    "select_minimum_motion_action": {
      "description": "Threshold every candidate residual, enumerate successful rows, and select the successful row with minimum absolute actuator motion.",
      "required_source_roles": [
        "candidate_rows_path",
        "residual_field",
        "action_field",
        "active_actuator_path",
        "allowed_values_path",
        "tolerance_path"
      ]
    },
    "simulate_paired_counterfactual": {
      "description": "Replay two registered optical states under the same action and return their exact responses, response difference, and centroid-direction preservation decision.",
      "required_source_roles": [
        "scenario_a_state_handle_path",
        "scenario_b_state_handle_path",
        "action_path",
        "changed_parameter_path"
      ]
    },
    "threshold_completion_directions": {
      "description": "Threshold every compatible-completion delta and return the set of observed directions and the first conflicting pair.",
      "required_source_roles": [
        "completion_rows_path",
        "delta_field",
        "threshold_path"
      ]
    }
  },
  "requested_operation": "compare exact sensor responses for two registered states under one shared action",
  "source_task": "counterfactual_reasoning"
}

Map each required role to a visible-evidence path. Return only strict JSON with tool_name and source_map; do not expose or guess private setup state.

